          "bytes": 738738,
          "sha256": "8fc20397ab5d514c119d7a025868414d78e436138d3867a4b7ba12334a72ec3a",
          "providerMd5": "b7435527d9628527ce47d89fc1468e9a"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/Models/jpg/1k/island_tree_02/island_tree_02_branches_diff_1k.jpg",
          "bytes": 528304,
          "sha256": "bee5ec22196e9e31ad0c95a5a9b4636571cc0124d5bb27a92f1e307d289cc60d",
          "providerMd5": "7792907fe2b2b748c129a2384192a579"
        }
      ],
      "changes": "Combined photographed leaf color and 16-bit source alpha into RGBA; single-leaf derivative cropped from the atlas. The GLB uses the original tree trunk/branches simplified offline, retaining referenced source positions/normals/UVs. To preserve complete leaves instead of pruning them into fragments, original 21-vertex leaves are fitted to local UV-to-position planes and represented by 2-triangle alpha cards. Deterministically retained 10,500 of 29,781 leaves and scaled each leaf by 1.684 for area compensation, preserving source positions/orientations/atlas layout. The result has 23,639 triangles with three material groups and original branch texture transform. Embedded trunk/branch photos use JPEG quality 90 without chroma subsampling; leaf color/alpha uses PNG with MASK 0.47. No runtime geometry codec or generative processing. Added a geometry-only distant LOD with 3,800 complete leaf cards (2.799x area-compensation scale) and the same trunk/branch geometry. The LOD keeps original local coordinates and three material names for binding the high-detail model materials; no duplicate textures are shipped.",
